# Third-party environment art, imported locally, NEVER committed.
#
# Content/CityPark/ is the Fab "City Park Environment Collection" (~1.5 GB), copied in from a
# local install of that pack -- see docs/citypark-level.md. It is licensed to Mike's Epic
# account, not to this repo: the Fab EULA grants use in projects, not redistribution of the raw
# assets, and this repo is PUBLIC. Committing it would be both a 1.5 GB binary blob in a repo
# whose rule is "never check binaries into git" and a licence breach. Anyone cloning this repo
# re-imports it themselves from their own Fab library.
#
# The level that USES it (Content/Maps/OB_City.umap) is small and IS committed -- it will show
# as a load error with unresolved references until the pack is imported, which is the intended
# and honest failure mode.
Content/CityPark/

# Content/Characters/Mannequins/ is Epic's template mannequin content (SKM_Manny_Simple + its skeleton,
# materials, textures and animations), shipped locally with every UE 5.7 install under
# Engine/../Templates/TemplateResources/High/Characters/Content/Mannequins/ -- see
# docs/mannequin-rider.md. It is licensed under the UE EULA as template content, not licensed for
# redistribution in an arbitrary public repo, and this repo is public: same reasoning as
# Content/CityPark/ above, not re-litigated here. ~126 MB, also fails the "never check binaries
# into git" rule on size alone. `ABoardActor`'s rider component (bShowRider) falls back
# gracefully -- board still renders, no rider, logged loudly -- if this directory is absent.
#
# NOTE THE PATH: Content/Characters/Mannequins/, not Content/Mannequins/. These packages record
# their own object paths as /Game/Characters/Mannequins/... internally, so importing them one
# level higher leaves every internal reference (skeleton, materials, rigs) dangling while the
# top-level assets still load by file path -- a rider that renders, in bind pose, with default
# materials, and a log line claiming an idle animation is playing. That was live for several
# captures. See docs/mannequin-rider.md.
Content/Characters/Mannequins/

# Content/MonoWheel_Board/ is the Fab pack "MonoWheel Board", licensed to Mike's Epic account.
# Same reasoning as Content/CityPark/ above -- the Fab EULA grants use in projects, not
# redistribution of the raw assets, and this repo is PUBLIC. Not re-litigated here.
#
# Only a 1.8 MB SUBSET is imported locally, not the 439 MB pack: the ten riding anim sequences,
# the Riding_BS blendspace, and the pack's own SK_Mannequin skeleton asset (161 KB) that those
# sequences are bound to. Deliberately NOT copied: the pack's AnimBPs (they pull their inputs
# through a Blueprint interface and call ACharacter APIs this project's rider does not have --
# we drive the blendspace from C++ instead), its board mesh, materials, textures, audio, maps,
# and the 397 MB Demo/ folder. See docs/rider-riding-animation.md for the import command.
#
# `ABoardActor` degrades in three tiers if this is absent -- riding blendspace, then the stock
# MM_Idle, then no rider at all -- so a clone without the pack still builds and still renders.
Content/MonoWheel_Board/

# macOS Finder noise.
.DS_Store
